<% content_for :title, @category.name %>

<%= page_header(
    title: @category.name,
    subtitle: "#{@category.category_type.titleize} category details and management",
    breadcrumbs: [
      { label: "Categories", url: categories_path(type: @category.category_type) },
      { label: @category.name }
    ],
    actions: [
      {
        label: "Manage Items",
        url: category_items_path(@category),
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded border border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-700 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-50 shadow-sm transition"
      },
      {
        label: "Edit",
        url: edit_category_path(@category),
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded border border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-700 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-50 shadow-sm transition"
      },
      {
        label: "Delete",
        url: category_path(@category),
        method: :delete,
        class: "inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded bg-status-danger text-white text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 shadow-sm transition",
        confirm: "Are you sure you want to delete #{@category.name}? This will permanently delete all #{@category.items.size} item(s) and #{@category.entries.size} entry/entries. This action cannot be undone."
      }
    ]
) %>

<div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-6">
  <%= render "categories/_partials/show/category_banner", category: @category %>

  <%= render "shared/period_toggle",
      monthly_path: category_path(@category),
      ytd_path: category_path(@category, period: "ytd") %>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    <%# THE CACHE NOW COVERS THE LEFT COLUMN ONLY, and the two pool cards are what pushed it there.

        It used to wrap both columns. Every figure inside it was derived from THIS category's own
        entries, and `Entry belongs_to :item, touch: true` / `Item belongs_to :category, touch: true`
        move `@category.updated_at` whenever one of those changes — so the key was sound for exactly
        the figures it held.

        An envelope's balance is not one of those. It moves when a distribution writes a
        `PoolMovement`, or when an entry in ANOTHER category pointing at the same pool is recorded,
        and neither of those touches this category: the block would have gone on printing last
        week's `$240.00 left` under a live "Rules on the Budget page" link. The same was already
        true of the pool card's progress bar beneath it. Both are now outside the cache, and the
        left column — the spending figures the period toggle is for — keeps it.

        Cheap: the right column costs two COUNTs and the five preloaded recent entries; the
        measured page cost is in the task report.

        AND THE POOL IS IN THE KEY, because moving the reader out was not available for the one
        that stayed (2d task 6). `_summary_card`'s savings arm prints
        `pool.calculator.{current_balance,progress_percentage}` from INSIDE the gray box in the
        middle of that partial — taking the reader outside this cache would have meant taking the
        box out of the card it is drawn in, which relocates the UI to fix a staleness bug. So the
        cache is keyed on the pool instead, which is the other half of the amendment's own offer
        and works because the bust chain exists on that side: `PoolMovement belongs_to :from_pool,
        touch: true` and `:to_pool, touch: true` move `pool.updated_at` on every distribution line
        and every reallocation, and `Category belongs_to :pool, touch: true` carries an entry's
        touch up through its item and its category to the pool — so an entry recorded in ANOTHER
        category on the same pool busts this one too.

        ONE HOLE STAYS AND IT IS NAMED: an entry carrying its own `pool_id` override touches its
        own category's pool, not the pool it was overridden onto, so an override entry against
        THIS pool from another category does not bust this key. It is narrower than what the key
        closes — the override lane is Task 5's, and no writer of it exists outside the entry form —
        and it is a pre-existing staleness rather than one this key introduces. Written down
        because the alternative is somebody re-deriving the guarantee and finding it wider than it
        is. %>
    <!-- Left Column -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6">
      <%# `pace_cache_key(selected_date)` left this key with the daily ramp it existed for: a
          prorated cap's "expected by today" figure changed every day, so the key had to as well.
          Proration is deleted (plan 3, task 3) and nothing under this cache moves with the clock. %>
      <% cache [@category, @category.pool, selected_date, current_period] do %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/summary_card", category: @category %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/items_list", category: @category %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <!-- Right Column -->
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <%= render "categories/_partials/show/details_card", category: @category %>

      <%# EVERY EXPENSE CATEGORY — spec §8.1's states, reduced to two by the cap's deletion. %>
      <% if @budget_block %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/budget_card", presenter: @budget_block %>
      <% end %>
      <% if @pool_card %>
        <%= render "categories/_partials/show/pool_card", presenter: @pool_card %>
      <% end %>

      <%= render "categories/_partials/show/recent_activity", category: @category %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
